===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Every time; always, without change.
#: {{ux|en|He is '''invariably''' late for meetings.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|IX|passage=“A tight little craft,” was Austin’s invariable comment on the matron;{{nb...}}. &para; Near her wandered her husband, orientally bland, '''invariably''' affable, and from time to time squinting sideways, as usual, in the ever-renewed expectation that he might catch a glimpse of his stiff, retroussé moustache.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=November|author=H. P. White|title=The Furka-Oberalp Railway|journal=Railway Magazine|page=770|text=In common with most Swiss Railways the standard of equipment and of operating efficiency is high, and stations and trains are '''invariably''' clean and well maintained.}}

